        <mxCell id="n160" value="Level 2: process 1.0 Transportation, ten subsectors" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=18;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#2C2C2A;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="20" width="1700" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n161" value="Balances with process 1.0 on Level 1. Stores 1.1 onward together make up D14 on Level 1, which process 5.0 reads to serve the map and analysts. Source IDs are from the Source Inventory. Rows are ordered so that subsectors that exchange data sit together; stand-alone subsectors come last. Sources enter each process from the left; what it produces is on the right. Green arrows are the links between processes: a store written by one process and read by another. Where a green link would have to cross another line, the store is repeated on the left of the reader with a dashed outline (same label = same store)." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5F5E5A;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="54" width="1700" height="50" as="geometry" />
