              <mxPoint x="1620" y="421" />
              <mxPoint x="990" y="421" />
            </Array>
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n582" value="&lt;b&gt;Shapes&lt;/b&gt;: grey square = external entity; purple circle = process; teal open rectangle = data store; arrow = data flow, labelled with the data it carries. Green arrow = a link between two processes through a store.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Rules&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. Every process has at least one input and one output.&lt;br&gt;2. No entity to entity, store to store, or entity to store without a process between.&lt;br&gt;3. Every store is written by a process and read by at least one somewhere in the model.&lt;br&gt;4. Every flow is labelled with a noun. On Level 1 a flow to or from a store takes the store&#39;s name.&lt;br&gt;5. Balancing: a child page has exactly the inputs and outputs of its parent process.&lt;br&gt;6. Numbering: 1.0 on L1, 1.1 to 1.10 on L2, 1.1.1 onward on L3. Stores: D1 to D16 on L1, D1.n per subsector, D1.1a per table.&lt;br&gt;7. Two processes are joined only when data really passes between them. Subsectors that share nothing are not joined.&lt;br&gt;8. Repeat a box rather than cross an arrow.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;To add a Level 3 page&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Duplicate the L3 TRN-01 page. Take the row for your subsector from its L2 page: those inputs and outputs are fixed. Replace the single process with capture processes (one per source), a matching or joining process, and one compute process per group of questions. Replace the subsector store with one store per table, and chain the processes through those stores.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Source Inventory column to DFD element&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Publisher = external entity. Grain = landing store and inbound flow label. Access method + Cadence = capture process. Question_Subsector_ID = the compute process the store feeds. Notes = uncertain or missing flows." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5F5E5A;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="600" width="1500" height="360" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
